<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Stocks quiet after Christmas Day.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Stocks quiet after Christmas Day.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks were very quiet in the after-hours trading session a day after Christmas, traders said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's been a very quiet afternoon,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said session one volume was 30,000 shares against 10,400 on Christmas Eve.</p>
<p>It said session two had 1,177,552 shares. There was no session two on December 24.</p>
<p>Markets were closed on December 25.</p>
